From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 10:00:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03969/11362] [outer-loop] L2 induction: env-gated CODE-ONLY
 truncation fix (works) reveals deeper degenerate-goal wall

The L2 induce prompt (with a WIN STATE exemplar) made Qwen3.5-9B burn its whole 4096-token
budget on win-state chain-of-thought before emitting code (stop_type=limit, 0 code), so
is_level_complete was never induced for ~10 milestones. Fix: a forceful CODE-ONLY directive +
stop=["```"] on the closing fence -> emits ONLY the code, 195 tokens / 15.6s (vs 450s truncated
/ 605s rambling), valid+satisfiable engine+is_level_complete in isolation. Wired end-to-end
through generate() (12.9s vs nothing). Env-gated CARNOT_ARC_CODEONLY_INDUCE=1, default OFF,
induce-scoped.

But on the LIVE lp85 graded-bias re-test the fixed induction still yields a DEGENERATE goal
(is_level_complete: return False) -> _goal_satisfiability_check returns degenerate_goal_predicate
-> lp85 stays L1. Truncation was one wall; goal-induction QUALITY is the deeper wall (and
reasoning-suppression may worsen the goal predicate specifically). Full A/B induction breakdown
pending. inference_substrate=live_llm_inference; solve_provenance=development_proxy;
verifier_is_oracle=false.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
